  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-97 (bundling), which is a substantive denial that requires an appeal to overturn. Since the payer offers peer-to-peer review and a denial is on the table, requesting a P2P is the most effective next step to challenge the bundling determination before filing a formal appeal. The prior P2P request likely did not resolve the issue or was not completed, so re-initiating or ensuring the P2P is active is the correct procedural move to progress the claim.",
